{
  "case_id": "2009-09-5201",
  "document_hash": "86d8765d626480a343400c05600d7611f6a0d8abee3948648b66f8b04cf7db56",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-09-5201",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "86d8765d626480a343400c05600d7611f6a0d8abee3948648b66f8b04cf7db56",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86d8765d6264-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The phrase \"term of imprisonment\" appears three times in the first sentence of the Federal good time statute. The first two times the parties are in agreement. \"Term of imprisonment\" means \"sentence imposed.\" The third use, which sets the rate for good time credit, also means the \"sentence imposed\" when it's used in the phrase \"up to 54 days of good time credit towards the service of the sentence.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-09-5201",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "86d8765d626480a343400c05600d7611f6a0d8abee3948648b66f8b04cf7db56",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86d8765d6264-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: But it doesn't always mean that. I think you say somewhere in your brief that it always means that. It surely does not always mean that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-09-5201",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "86d8765d626480a343400c05600d7611f6a0d8abee3948648b66f8b04cf7db56",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86d8765d6264-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The flaw in the Bureau of Prisons system is that they do not give credit towards the term of imprisonment as this statute in 3624(b) dictates."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-09-5201",
      "confidence": 0.88,
      "document_hash": "86d8765d626480a343400c05600d7611f6a0d8abee3948648b66f8b04cf7db56",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86d8765d6264-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, I'm -- perhaps I can, if you will permit me, rephrase Justice Alito's question in sort of the more simplistic way I looked at it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-09-5201",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "86d8765d626480a343400c05600d7611f6a0d8abee3948648b66f8b04cf7db56",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86d8765d6264-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: I take it what you want is you, in -- in essence, want him to get credit for 54 days for that tenth year?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. SADY",
      "case_id": "2009-09-5201",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "86d8765d626480a343400c05600d7611f6a0d8abee3948648b66f8b04cf7db56",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86d8765d6264-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SADY: Justice Ginsburg, there are approximately 200,000 prisoners, and of those about 195,000 of them are eligible for good time credits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-09-5201",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "86d8765d626480a343400c05600d7611f6a0d8abee3948648b66f8b04cf7db56",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86d8765d6264-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Let me interrupt and get one thing off my mind that I just -- supposing he misbehaves in year 3. Does that just affect his good time credits in year 3, or does it mean he is canceled for years 1 and 2?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2009-09-5201",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86d8765d626480a343400c05600d7611f6a0d8abee3948648b66f8b04cf7db56",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86d8765d6264-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We -- if we disagree with that, if we disagree that the BOP has authority in this area, then -- as Justice Ginsburg's question, I think, suggests -- does not the Rule of Lenity apply?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2009-09-5201",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86d8765d626480a343400c05600d7611f6a0d8abee3948648b66f8b04cf7db56",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86d8765d6264-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, how do you explain the Granderson case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Sady",
      "case_id": "2009-09-5201",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "86d8765d626480a343400c05600d7611f6a0d8abee3948648b66f8b04cf7db56",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86d8765d6264-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Court in -- in Lynce and in Weaver used the term \"increase in punishment\" when there was no longer available good time credit. For -- to say that somebody has to serve 87.2 percent of the term of imprisonment imposed by the judge instead of 85 percent, that is imprisonment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-09-5201",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "86d8765d626480a343400c05600d7611f6a0d8abee3948648b66f8b04cf7db56",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86d8765d6264-0003-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
